k:prose-invert" data-page-title=3D"Memory overview" data-page-href=3D"/oss/=
python/concepts/memory" id=3D"content"><span data-as=3D"p"><a class=3D"link=
" href=3D"https://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/langgraph/add-memory">Memor=
y</a> is a system that remembers information about previous interactions. F=
or AI agents, memory is crucial because it lets them remember previous inte=
ractions, learn from feedback, and adapt to user preferences. As agents tac=
kle more complex tasks with numerous user interactions, this capability bec=
omes essential for both efficiency and user satisfaction.</span>
<span data-as=3D"p">This conceptual guide covers two types of memory, based=
 on their recall scope:</span>
<ul>
<li><a href=3D"https://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/concepts/memory#short-=
term-memory" class=3D"link">Short-term memory</a>, or <a class=3D"link" hre=
f=3D"https://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/langgraph/persistence#threads">t=
hread</a>-scoped memory, tracks the ongoing conversation by maintaining mes=
sage history within a session. LangGraph manages short-term memory as a par=
t of your agent=E2=80=99s <a class=3D"link" href=3D"https://docs.langchain.=
com/oss/python/langgraph/graph-api#state">state</a>. State is persisted to =
a database using a <a class=3D"link" href=3D"https://docs.langchain.com/oss=
/python/langgraph/persistence#checkpoints">checkpointer</a> so the thread c=
an be resumed at any time. Short-term memory updates when the graph is invo=
ked or a step is completed, and the State is read at the start of each step=
.</li>
<li><a href=3D"https://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/concepts/memory#long-t=
erm-memory" class=3D"link">Long-term memory</a> stores user-specific or app=
lication-level data across sessions and is shared <em>across</em> conversat=
ional threads. It can be recalled <em>at any time</em> and <em>in any threa=
d</em>. Memories are scoped to any custom namespace, not just within a sing=
le thread ID. LangGraph provides <a class=3D"link" href=3D"https://docs.lan=
gchain.com/oss/python/langgraph/persistence#memory-store">stores</a> (<a hr=
ef=3D"https://langchain-ai.github.io/langgraph/reference/store/#langgraph.s=
tore.base.BaseStore" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noreferrer" class=3D"link">re=
ference doc</a>) to let you save and recall long-term memories.</li>
</ul>
