<span data-as=3D"p"><a class=3D"link" href=3D"https://docs.langchain.com/os=
s/python/langgraph/add-memory#add-short-term-memory">Short-term memory</a> =
lets your application remember previous interactions within a single <a cla=
ss=3D"link" href=3D"https://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/langgraph/persist=
ence#threads">thread</a> or conversation. A <a class=3D"link" href=3D"https=
://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/langgraph/persistence#threads">thread</a> =
organizes multiple interactions in a session, similar to the way email grou=
ps messages in a single conversation.</span>
<span data-as=3D"p">LangGraph manages short-term memory as part of the agen=
t=E2=80=99s state, persisted via thread-scoped checkpoints. This state can =
normally include the conversation history along with other stateful data, s=
uch as uploaded files, retrieved documents, or generated artifacts. By stor=
ing these in the graph=E2=80=99s state, the bot can access the full context=
 for a given conversation while maintaining separation between different th=
reads.</span>
