<span data-as=3D"p">Memories can be a single, continuously updated =E2=80=
=9Cprofile=E2=80=9D of well-scoped and specific information about a user, o=
rganization, or other entity (including the agent itself). A profile is gen=
erally just a JSON document with various key-value pairs you=E2=80=99ve sel=
ected to represent your domain.</span>
<span data-as=3D"p">When remembering a profile, you will want to make sure =
that you are <strong>updating</strong> the profile each time. As a result, =
you will want to pass in the previous profile and <a href=3D"https://github=
.com/langchain-ai/memory-template" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noreferrer" cla=
ss=3D"link">ask the model to generate a new profile</a> (or some <a href=3D=
"https://github.com/hinthornw/trustcall" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noreferre=
r" class=3D"link">JSON patch</a> to apply to the old profile). This can be =
become error-prone as the profile gets larger, and may benefit from splitti=
ng a profile into multiple documents or <strong>strict</strong> decoding wh=
en generating documents to ensure the memory schemas remains valid.</span>
